{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q13536972","formula":"C₂₃H₄₈","hill":"C23H48","elements":["H","C"],"composition":{"C":23.0,"H":48.0},"names":{"en":"Evenkite","ru":"Эвенкит","uk":"Евенкіт"},"descriptions":{"en":"Evenkite is a rare hydrocarbon mineral with formula C24H50; specifically, H3C–(CH2)22–CH3, the alkane n-tetracosane. It occurs as very soft (Mohs hardness 1) transparent crystals, colorless to yellow, with a waxy luster. The softness is a characteristic of crystalline long-chain alkanes, which are the main constituents of paraffin wax.","ru":"Эвенкит (англ. Evenkite) — органический минерал, смесь гомологов предельных углеводородов. Назван по месту первой находки в Эвенкии.","uk":"Евенкіт — органічний мінерал. Суміш гомологів парафінових вуглеводнів. Уперше відкритий у Евенкії на Хавокиперських скелях (район р."},"fame":13,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q13536972","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evenkite","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%AD%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D0%B8%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%95%D0%B2%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%BA%D1%96%D1%82","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"photo","name":"Wikimedia Commons","url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Evenkite-444375.jpg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 de"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q150843","formula":"C₁₆H₃₄","names":{"en":"Hexadecane","ru":"Гексадекан","uk":"Гексадекан"},"elements":["H","C"],"fame":39,"kind":"molecule"},{"id":"Q150788","formula":"C₁₃H₂₈","names":{"en":"Tridecane","ru":"Т